      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'm trying to understand how this relates to nutrient retention. If this \"substitution\" creates a negative charge that pulls in cations, what happens to the efficiency of that exchange if the soil becomes highly acidic and the concentration of H+ ions increases? Does the acidity fundamentally change how these cations are held by the lattice?",
